      "id": 1,
      "text": "Walburg, originally Concordia, is a German community 33 miles northeast of Austin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/walburg-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was renamed after Walburg, Germany, when a post office was added in 1886.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/walburg-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Zion Lutheran parochial school, established in 1882, sits next to the church and has long history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wilcotx.gov/893/Walburg"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Walburg’s historic buildings from the late 1890s have made it a filming location for movies like The Texas Chain Saw Massacre 2.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walburg%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Two Lutheran churches—one LCMS, one LCMC—serve the community, reflecting its German heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
